---
source: crates/cache-explorer-core/tests/golden.rs
description: "4-byte words: four to a line; the largest word, 4,294,967,295, stored and loaded."
---
1.1 | decode | lineSize | - | - | Store 0x0A8: tag 0x01, set 2, offset 8 (word 2).
1.2 | miss | associativity | accesses, stores, misses | - | Set 2 is invalid. Miss.
1.3 | victim | associativity | - | - | Set 2 has one way; the line goes there.
1.4 | fill | lineSize | valid 2/0, tag 2/0, word 2/0/0, word 2/0/1, word 2/0/2, word 2/0/3, fills | - | Fill way 0 with line 0x0A0–0x0AF from memory.
1.5 | write | writePolicy | dirty 2/0, word 2/0/2 | - | Write 4,294,967,295 into word 2 of way 0 and set its dirty bit. Memory at 0x0A8 is now stale.
2.1 | decode | lineSize | - | - | Load 0x0A8: tag 0x01, set 2, offset 8 (word 2).
2.2 | hit | associativity | accesses, loads, hits | - | Set 2, way 0: valid, and tag 0x01 matches. Hit.
2.3 | complete | - | r1 | - | Read word 2 of way 0 (4,294,967,295) into r1.
